{"symbol":"ATC.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T19:47:12Z","info":{"address1":"Östra Hamngatan 30-34","city":"Gothenburg","zip":"411 09","country":"Sweden","phone":"46 10 45 18 000","website":"https://www.arcticpaper.com","industry":"Paper & Paper Products","industryKey":"paper-paper-products","industryDisp":"Paper & Paper Products","sector":"Basic Materials","sectorKey":"basic-materials","sectorDisp":"Basic Materials","longBusinessSummary":"Arctic Paper S.A., together with its subsidiaries, produces paper and pulp in Poland, Germany, France, the United Kingdom, Scandinavia, the rest of Western Europe, Central and Eastern Europe, and internationally. It operates the through Paper and Pulp segments. The Paper segment offers uncoated paper for printing or other graphic purposes, including wood-free and wood-containing paper, as well as coated paper, a wood-free paper for printing or other graphic purposes, one-side or two-side coated with mixtures containing mineral pigments, such as China clay, calcium carbonate, etc. The Pulp segment provides bleached sulphate pulp and unbleached sulphate pulp to produce printing and writing papers, cardboard, toilet paper, white packaging paper, and chemi-thermo mechanical pulp to produce printing and writing paper. The company is also involved in the production of packaging; generation, transmission, and distribution of electricity; heat production and distribution; paper and pulp distribution; provision of logistics services; production of hydropower; and energy storage business. It markets its products under the Munken, Arctic Volume, G, and Amber brands. The company was founded in 1740 and is headquartered in Gothenburg, Sweden. Arctic Paper S.A. operates as a subsidiary of Nemus Holding AB.","fullTimeEmployees":1500,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Michal Piotr Jarczynski","age":57,"title":"President of Management Board & CEO","yearBorn":1968,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":2701732,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercis